  <static seed="53" source="Library/272/setStewart12_5/problem_2.pg">
    <statement><p>Find the vector and parametric equations for the line through the point
P(4, 2, 4) and parallel to the vector 
<m>0\mathbf i  - 3\mathbf j  - 3\mathbf k</m>.</p>
<p>Vector Form: <m>\mathbf r = \langle</m><fillin characters="10" name="AnSwEr0001"/>, <fillin characters="10" name="AnSwEr0002"/>, 4 <m>\rangle + t \langle</m>
<fillin characters="10" name="AnSwEr0003"/>, <fillin characters="10" name="AnSwEr0004"/>, -3 <m>\rangle</m></p>
<p>Parametric form (parameter t, and passing through P when t = 0):</p>
<p><m>x = x(t) =</m><fillin characters="30" name="AnSwEr0005"/></p>
<p><m>y = y(t) =</m><fillin characters="30" name="AnSwEr0006"/></p>
<p><m>z = z(t) =</m><fillin characters="30" name="AnSwEr0007"/></p>
</statement>
    <answer>
      <p>
        <m>4</m>
      </p>
    </answer>
    <answer>
      <p>
        <m>2</m>
      </p>
    </answer>
    <answer>
      <p>
        <m>0</m>
      </p>
    </answer>
    <answer>
      <p>
        <m>-3</m>
      </p>
    </answer>
    <answer>
      <p>
        <m>4+t\cdot 0</m>
      </p>
    </answer>
    <answer>
      <p>
        <m>2+t\mathopen{}\left(-3\right)</m>
      </p>
    </answer>
    <answer>
      <p>
        <m>4+t\mathopen{}\left(-3\right)</m>
      </p>
    </answer>
